   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Infinite Marquee\n\nA continuously scrolling horizontal text strip that loops seamlessly.\n\nCategory: typography. Length: 6 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- A scene needs ambient motion in the background or as a decorative band between sections.\n- Looping brand words, feature names, or a tagline should scroll continuously without a start or end.\n\nAvoid when:\n- The text should enter, hold, then exit: use blur-out-up or mask-reveal-up.\n- You need 3D perspective depth on the strip: use perspective-marquee.\n- The marquee should stop on a specific word: this one loops forever.\n\nVariables:\n- text (string): Text, default \"ship \\u00b7 build \\u00b7 animate \\u00b7 \"\n- font_size (number, 12-240): Font size, default 120\n- color (color): Color, default \"#171717\"\n- font_weight (enum): Font weight, default \"700\"\n- pixels_per_frame (number, 1-30): Pixels per frame, default 4\n- stroke (boolean): Stroke, default false\n- stroke_color (color): Stroke color, default \"#171717\"\n- speed (number, 0.25-4): Speed, default 1\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
  {
   "path": "scene.html",
   "role": "source",
   "content": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  Infinite Marquee\n\n  A continuously scrolling horizontal text strip that loops seamlessly.\n\n  Ported to an HTML + GSAP sub-composition by usemosio/blocks from:\n  https://github.com/Remocn/remocn/blob/126221ae00ba86eb40b65731b125ff398687d3b7/registry/remocn/infinite-marquee/index.tsx\n\n  MIT License\n\n  Copyright (c) 2026 Remocn\n\n  Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\n  of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\n  in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\n  to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\n  copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\n  furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\n  The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\n  copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\n  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\n  IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\n  FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\n  AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\n  LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\n  OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\n  SOFTWARE.\n-->\n<html\n  lang=\"en\"\n  data-composition-id=\"infinite-marquee\"\n  data-composition-duration=\"6\"\n  data-composition-variables='[\n    {\"id\": \"text\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Text\", \"description\": \"Text that repeats along the strip.\", \"default\": \"ship · build · animate · \"},\n    {\"id\": \"font_size\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Font size\", \"description\": \"Text size in pixels.\", \"default\": 120, \"min\": 12, \"max\": 240, \"step\": 1, \"unit\": \"px\"},\n    {\"id\": \"color\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Color\", \"description\": \"Text color.\", \"default\": \"#171717\"},\n    {\"id\": \"font_weight\", \"type\": \"enum\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Font weight\", \"description\": \"Weight of the text.\", \"default\": \"700\", \"options\": [{\"value\": \"400\", \"label\": \"Regular\"}, {\"value\": \"500\", \"label\": \"Medium\"}, {\"value\": \"600\", \"label\": \"Semibold\"}, {\"value\": \"700\", \"label\": \"Bold\"}]},\n    {\"id\": \"pixels_per_frame\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Pixels per frame\", \"description\": \"Scroll speed at 30 fps.\", \"default\": 4, \"min\": 1, \"max\": 30, \"step\": 1, \"unit\": \"px\"},\n    {\"id\": \"stroke\", \"type\": \"boolean\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Stroke\", \"description\": \"Outline the letters instead of filling them.\", \"default\": false},\n    {\"id\": \"stroke_color\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Stroke color\", \"description\": \"Outline color when Stroke is on.\", \"default\": \"#171717\"},\n    {\"id\": \"speed\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Speed\", \"description\": \"Playback speed multiplier.\", \"default\": 1, \"min\": 0.25, \"max\": 4, \"step\": 0.05, \"unit\": \"x\"}\n  ]'\n>\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <title>Infinite Marquee</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <template>\n      <link\n        rel=\"stylesheet\"\n        href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Geist:wght@400;500;600;700&amp;display=block\"\n      />\n      <style>\n        #root {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          overflow: hidden;\n          container-type: size;\n          pointer-events: none;\n        }\n        .mq-stage { position: absolute; inset: 0; display: flex; align-items: center; overflow: hidden; }\n        .mq-strip { display: flex; white-space: nowrap; will-change: transform; font-family: var(--font-display, Geist, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, sans-serif); letter-spacing: -0.03em; line-height: 1.2; }\n        .mq-item { padding-right: 0.4em; }\n      </style>\n\n      <div id=\"root\" data-composition-id=\"infinite-marquee\" data-duration=\"6\" data-fps=\"30\">\n        <div id=\"mq-clip\" class=\"mq-stage clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"6\" data-track-index=\"0\">\n          <div id=\"mq-strip\" class=\"mq-strip\"></div>\n        </div>\n\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/CustomEase.min.js\"></script>\n        <script>\n          (function () {\n            \"use strict\";\n\n            var root = document.getElementById(\"root\");\n            var vars =\n              window.__hyperframes && window.__hyperframes.getVariables\n                ? window.__hyperframes.getVariables()\n                : {};\n            function num(value, fallback, min, max) {\n              var n = Number(value);\n              return Number.isFinite(n) ? Math.min(max, Math.max(min, n)) : fallback;\n            }\n            function str(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"string\" && value.trim() ? value : fallback;\n            }\n            function pick(value, options, fallback) {\n              return options.indexOf(String(value)) >= 0 ? String(value) : fallback;\n            }\n            function col(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"string\" && value ? value : fallback;\n            }\n            function bool(value, fallback) {\n              if (typeof value === \"boolean\") return value;\n              if (value === \"true\") return true;\n              if (value === \"false\") return false;\n              return fallback;\n            }\n            function fit(el, maxPx, size, ratio) {\n              // Shrink el's font size until its scrollWidth fits ratio of the frame width.\n              el.style.fontSize = size + \"px\";\n              var max = Math.max(1, root.clientWidth * (ratio || 0.9));\n              if (el.scrollWidth > max) { size = Math.max(10, size * (max / el.scrollWidth)); el.style.fontSize = size + \"px\"; }\n              return size;\n            }\n            gsap.registerPlugin(CustomEase);\n            function ease(name, a, b, c, d) { return CustomEase.create(name, \"M0,0 C\" + a + \",\" + b + \" \" + c + \",\" + d + \" 1,1\"); }\n            function mulberry32(a) { return function () { a |= 0; a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) | 0; var t = Math.imul(a ^ (a >>> 15), 1 | a); t = (t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), 61 | t)) ^ t; return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296; }; }\n            var tl = gsap.timeline({ paused: true });\n            var TOTAL = parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"6\");\n            function ip(t, a, b, from, to, e) {\n              var p = b === a ? 1 : (t - a) / (b - a);\n              p = Math.min(1, Math.max(0, p));\n              if (e) p = e(p);\n              return from + (to - from) * p;\n            }\n            function hash01(seed) {\n              var h = 2166136261;\n              for (var i = 0; i < seed.length; i++) { h ^= seed.charCodeAt(i); h = Math.imul(h, 16777619); }\n              h = Math.imul(h ^ (h >>> 13), 2246822519);\n              return ((h ^ (h >>> 16)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;\n            }\n            function hashRange(seed, lo, hi) { return lo + hash01(seed) * (hi - lo); }\n            // Snap a frame number down to a stop-motion pose.\n            function qf(frame, step) { return Math.floor(frame / step + 1e-6) * step; }\n            function kf(t, keys, vals, e) {\n              if (t <= keys[0]) return vals[0];\n              for (var i = 0; i < keys.length - 1; i++) if (t <= keys[i + 1]) return ip(t, keys[i], keys[i + 1], vals[i], vals[i + 1], e);\n              return vals[vals.length - 1];\n            }\n            // Per-frame drawing: a pure function of the timeline time, run from a tween's onUpdate.\n            function tick(draw) {\n              tl.to({}, { duration: TOTAL, ease: \"none\", onUpdate: function () { draw(tl.time()); } }, 0);\n              draw(0);\n            }\n            var cubOut = ease(\"cub-out\", 0.215, 0.61, 0.355, 1);\n            var cubIn = ease(\"cub-in\", 0.55, 0.055, 0.675, 0.19);\n            var cubInOut = ease(\"cub-io\", 0.645, 0.045, 0.355, 1);\n\n            var strip = document.getElementById(\"mq-strip\");\n            var text = str(vars.text, \"ship · build · animate · \");\n            var size = num(vars.font_size, 120, 12, 240);\n            var ppf = num(vars.pixels_per_frame, 4, 1, 30);\n            var speed = num(vars.speed, 1, 0.25, 4);\n            var stroke = bool(vars.stroke, false);\n            var color = col(vars.color, \"#171717\");\n            strip.style.fontSize = size + \"px\";\n            strip.style.fontWeight = pick(vars.font_weight, [\"400\", \"500\", \"600\", \"700\"], \"700\");\n            function item() {\n              var s = document.createElement(\"span\");\n              s.className = \"mq-item\";\n              s.textContent = text;\n              s.style.color = stroke ? \"transparent\" : color;\n              if (stroke) s.style.webkitTextStroke = \"2px \" + col(vars.stroke_color, \"#171717\");\n              strip.appendChild(s);\n              return s;\n            }\n            var first = item();\n            var period = Math.max(1, first.getBoundingClientRect().width);\n            var copies = Math.ceil(root.clientWidth / period) + 2;\n            for (var i = 1; i < copies; i++) item();\n            // The strip starts centred on the frame, as in remocn, and scrolls left by exactly one repeat per loop.\n            var base = (root.clientWidth - period * copies) / 2;\n            tick(function (t) {\n              var off = -((t * 30 * speed * ppf) % period);\n              gsap.set(strip, { x: base + off });\n            });\n            var total = parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"6\");\n            if (tl.duration() < total) tl.to({}, { duration: total - tl.duration() });\n            tl.seek(0);\n            window.__timelines = window.__timelines || {};\n            window.__timelines[\"infinite-marquee\"] = tl;\n          })();\n        </script>\n      </div>\n    </template>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
  }
 ],
